Subject: [PATCH] test: settle owned Host writes before fixture reopen and
 cleanup

Owner request: TODO delivery 0 deterministic verification, OV-112 and P12.

Reason: the full delivery gate on 859ed22a failed with ENOTEMPTY while
cleaning artifacts/session after the public automatic-decision Stop case.
The shared Pi Host fixture closed SQLite and removed its directory after
beginShutdown without awaiting owned receipt writers.

Reuse production's existing waitForShutdownSettlement before closing the
fixture store on both reopen and close. Add held-writer regressions with
real SQLite/filesystem, and release the whiteboard's fake approval in
finally so assertion failures cannot strand cleanup.

Current upstream v3.15.1 does not contain this Fleet-owned Pi fixture.
No production runtime, dependency, account, permission or data format changes.
